Known schema inconsistencies currently exist.

Pay particular attention to:

`docutracker_notifications`

The fresh-install schema may not contain fields expected by later code/migrations, including:

- `read_at`
- `channel`
- `delivery_status`
- `sent_at`
- `failed_at`
- `failure_reason`

Also:

`docutracker_document_files`

may exist through migrations but not the fresh-install schema.

Before editing related functionality:

- compare migrations
- compare init-schema
- compare runtime queries
- identify the intended final schema

Do not silently work around schema drift only in Flutter.

