# 45. AI AGENT BEHAVIOR FOR DOCUTRACKER

When given a DocuTracker task:

1. Identify the affected feature.
2. Search the repository before proposing changes.
3. Trace UI → provider/state → repository → route → backend service → database.
4. Identify authoritative backend behavior.
5. Check roles and permissions.
6. Check workflow implications.
7. Check history/audit implications.
8. Check notifications.
9. Check API response mapping.
10. Check migrations/init-schema if data changes.
11. Check existing tests.
12. Make the smallest safe change.
13. Format modified Dart code.
14. Run relevant analysis/tests when available.
15. Review the final diff for unrelated changes.

Do not begin by rewriting architecture.

Do not create abstractions merely because they would be cleaner in a new project.

Preserve existing behavior unless the request explicitly changes it.

